within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.R_RespiratorySystem.R03B_OtherDrugsForObstructiveAirwayDiseasesInhalants.R03BA02_Budesonide;
model Budesonide_Lnnebo2007_PD_acth
  "indirect_response_i exposure-response sweep — Lönnebo_2007 :: ACTH (ACTH)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Interfaces.PartialExposureResponseSweep(
    E0 = 2.58e-09,      // [mol/m3; pmol l-1 × 1e-09]
    Emax = 1,  // type I effect term
    EC50 = 0.000325,  // [kg/m3; mg l-1 × 0.001]
    gamma = 1,
    exposure_per_s = 0.001);   // 1 mg l-1 per second
equation
  response = E0*(1 - Emax*frac);   // steady state, indirect response type I
  // defaulted: gamma
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 3.3, Interval = 0.0066),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Budesonide_Lnnebo2007_PD_acth</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Lönnebo A et al., <i>British journal of clinical pharmacology 64(2):125–132</i> 2007 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-2125.2007.02867.x\">doi:10.1111/j.1365-2125.2007.02867.x</a>) — ACTH [pmol l-1] against budesonide mg l-1 — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: indirect_response_i.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =       2.58 pmol l-1 drug-free response (baseline) (Baseline ACTH, Q324)
  Emax  =          1          maximal effect term (I max, Q323)
  EC50  =      0.325 mg l-1   exposure at half of the maximal effect term (IC 50,1 and 2, Q322)
  gamma = (library default) Hill coefficient</pre><p>The algebra is <code>response = E0*(1 - Emax*frac)</code>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one mg l-1 of budesonide per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 2.58e-09   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (0.325 mg l-1)  response 1.29e-09
  exposure -> infinity  response 0</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Lönnebo_2007: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: accepted with caveats</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Budesonide_Lnnebo2007_PD_acth;
